# How to cite the map. GitHub reads this file for its "Cite this repository" button,
# and scripts/build.py reads it for the "How to cite" block at the foot of every page.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the feature-learning map (its statements, its regime grid or its experiments),
  please cite it as below, with the version you used. For any result taken from the map,
  also cite the original paper: the map restates published results, and the papers are the sources.
title: Feature-learning literature map
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Göring
    given-names: Niclas
url: https://niclasgoering.github.io/feature-learning-map/
repository-code: https://github.com/NiclasGoering/feature-learning-map
abstract: >-
  A public map of the theory literature on feature learning in neural networks, for Bayesian
  posteriors and gradient-based training: papers with structured entries, the main statements
  rewritten in one notation, a regime grid, mechanisms, open problems and the map's own
  numerical experiments.
keywords:
  - feature learning
  - Bayesian neural networks
  - neural network theory
  - literature map
preferred-citation:
  type: website
  title: Feature-learning literature map
  authors:
    - family-names: Göring
      given-names: Niclas
  year: 2026
  url: https://niclasgoering.github.io/feature-learning-map/
